---
<DocsLayout title="Menu Reference" description="Every Ravenburst menu item, what it does, and its keyboard shortcut.">
  <h1>Menu Reference</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every menu, item by item. Shortcuts are shown for Windows and Linux; on a Mac use <kbd>⌘</kbd> for <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> and <kbd>⌥</kbd> for <kbd>Alt</kbd> (see <a href="/docs/keyboard-shortcuts">Keyboard Shortcuts</a> for the exceptions).</p>
  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Menus">
    <p>Menus</p>
    <ul>
      {menus.map((m) => <li><a href={`#${m.id}`}>{m.name}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  {menus.map((m) => (
    <section>
      <h2 id={m.id}>{m.name}</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Shortcut</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {m.rows.map(([item, what, keys]) => (
              <tr><td class="menu">{item}</td><td>{what}</td><td>{keys ? <kbd>{keys}</kbd> : ''}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
  <p>On a Mac, Preferences and Quit are also in the <span class="menu">Ravenburst</span> menu.</p>
</DocsLayout>
